.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt DOAS-COMMON 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm doas-common
.Nd multicall binary for doas, doasedit and sudo
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Op Fl v | Fl -version
.Op Fl l | Fl -list
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
binary contains three applets.
The applet is selected by the last component of the invoked path
.Pq Dv argv\[u005B]0\[u005D] :
.Bl -tag -width doasedit
.It Sy doas
Execute a command as another user; see
.Xr doas 1 .
.It Sy doasedit
Edit files as root using an unprivileged editor; see
.Xr doasedit 1 .
.It Sy sudo
Translate a sudo command line into doas arguments and run it; see
.Xr sudo 1 .
.El
.Pp
Invoked as
.Nm
itself, or under any other name, no applet runs and only the options below are
accepted.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl l , Fl -list
Print the applets and what they do, one tab separated name and description per
line, and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std doas-common
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr doas 1 ,
.Xr doasedit 1 ,
.Xr sudo 1 ,
.Xr doas.conf 5
